    {
      "title": "Mono-First Typography Philosophy",
      "content": "The system commits to a single monospace voice across every context — display, body, caption, button, timestamp. This is a deliberate anti-marketing choice: the site looks less like a portfolio and more like a working tool, a terminal, or a developer's personal homepage. The only escape is a secondary Helvetica at 44px light (weight 300) for occasional humanist contrast, never as the dominant voice. Headlines at 43px in IBM Plex Mono 400 are intentionally un-bold: the mono rhythm does the work of hierarchy, not weight. Never substitute a proportional sans for body text — the entire interface is calibrated to the monospace character grid."
