    {
      "title": "The Highlighted-Letter Game",
      "content": "The single most distinctive micro-interaction: a flat color block (#f9f5a2 yellow or #c7f6ff cyan) sits behind exactly one character in an otherwise normal word. Used in 'School is (y)our creative studio.' — only the 'y' is highlighted. The technique treats a single letter as a swappable variable and signals 'this is yours to change'. The highlight block has zero padding offset, no rounded corners, sits at glyph baseline. This is not a link, not a button — it's a typographic emphasis that says 'customize here' without ever using the word."
